{{also|Cinnamon}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Canelle Cinnamomum burmannii Luc Viatour.jpg|thumb|225px|Sticks of {{taxlink|Cinnamomum burmanni|species}}]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|synamome}}, from {{der|en|fro|cinnamone}}, from {{der|en|la|cinnamon}}, {{m|la|cinnamomum}}, from {{der|en|grc|κιννάμωμον}}, later {{m|grc|κίνναμον}}, according to Herodotus from {{der|en|phn}}, cognate with {{cog|he|קִנָּמוֹן|tr=qinnāmōn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɪn.ə.mən/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɪn.ə.mən/|/ˈsɪn.ə.mɪn/|a=US,Canada}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-cinnamon.ogg|a=US}}
** {{qualifier|nonstandard}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɪ.mɪn/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪmɪn|s=2|q1=nonstandard}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[small]] [[evergreen]] [[tree]] native to [[Sri Lanka]] and [[south]]ern [[India]], {{taxfmt|Cinnamomum verum|species}} or ''[[Cinnamomum zeylanicum]]'', belonging to the family {{taxfmt|Lauraceae|family}}.
# Several [[related]] [[tree]]s, notably the [[Indonesian cinnamon]] ({{taxlink|Cinnamomum burmanni|species}}) and [[Chinese cinnamon]] or [[cassia]] ({{taxlink|Cinnamomum aromaticum|species}} or {{taxfmt|Cinnamomum cassia|species}}).
# {{lb|en|mostly|uncountable}} A [[spice]] from the [[dried]] [[aromatic]] [[bark]] of the cinnamon tree, either [[roll]]ed into [[strip]]s or [[grind|ground]] into a [[powder]]. The word is commonly used as [[trade name]] for spices made of any of the species above.
## {{vern|true cinnamon}}, the [[product]] made of {{taxfmt|Cinnamomum verum|species}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[warm]] [[yellow]]ish-[[brown]] [[color]], the color of cinnamon.
#: {{color panel|8A563A}}

